- Factory image: document the `pkg/iso/customize.go` console routing change for Raspberry Pi/QEMU images and harden the signed HTTP boot EEPROM runbook.
- Create docker pxe-server
- Iterate on docker platform builder and runtime containers
- Create docker ansible execution environment
- Make DNS forwarders optional, remove public forwarding from configs
- Create docker trusted-platform-iso-builder to build custom ISO w/ custom secure boot keys
- Start integration with libvirt and docker to perform automated provisioning of compute
  instances and deployment orchestration.
- Create ansible playbooks to support docker, k3s and podman deployment environments
- Integrate ansible playbooks with trusted-platform-iso-builder first boot script
- Enable LUKS full drive encryption via ISO installer preseed
- systemd-cryptenroll integration started but encountered bug on debian/ubuntu:
  - https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/cryptsetup/+bug/1980018
  - https://answers.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+question/702266
  - https://salsa.debian.org/cryptsetup-team/cryptsetup/-/merge_requests/39/diffs#00524e372ebef34fc25a9ccf26625e53d9a78a00
- Add more documentation
- Remove support for 32-bit architectures
- Remove hard coded sha256 PCR bank and NameAlg references from tpm2 package
- Add TPM_PT_NV_BUFFER_MAX to tpm2 capabilities info 
- Protected memory: rename the locked-memory primitive `pkg/memguard.Secret` to
  `MemoryEnclave` and migrate every in-repo caller. `Secret`, `New`,
  `NewFromString`, `NewRandom` and `MemoryEnclave.WithBytes` remain as
  deprecated aliases and are removed in the coordinated portfolio-wide
  protected-memory wave. See docs/security/protected-memory.md.
- Protected memory: hold PIV PINs and imported private key material in a
  `MemoryEnclave` across all five transports. `PIVGenerateRequest.PIN`,
  `PIVSignRequest.PIN`, `PIVImportRequest.PIN` and
  `PIVImportRequest.PrivateKeyPEM` are deprecated in favour of `PINEnclave` /
  `PrivateKey`, read through `WithPIN` / `WithPrivateKeyPEM`. The plain field
  is read only when no enclave was supplied; a destroyed enclave fails closed
  with `memguard.ErrDestroyed`. The wire contract is unchanged.
